<title>USA: Sparks said to peg U.S. corn 8.955 bln, soy 2.310.</title>
<headline>Sparks said to peg U.S. corn 8.955 bln, soy 2.310.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis analytical firm Sparks Companies was said to have estimated 1996 U.S. corn production at 8.955 billion bushels and soybean production at 2.310 billion, industry sources said.</p>
<p>USDA on Sept 11 put U.S. corn output at 8.804 billion and the soybean crop at 2.270 billion.</p>
<p>Sparks Companies officials were not available for comment.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720</p>
